# {{ project_name }}

{{ description }}

An asynchronous FastAPI service with SQLModel persistence, typed settings, structured errors,
request IDs, and deny-by-default host and CORS policies.

## Requirements

[uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) is the only tool you need. It installs Python {{ python_version }}+
and every development tool on demand, on Windows, macOS, and Linux.

## Getting started

```bash
uv sync                                        # create .venv with the dev group
uv lock                                        # create uv.lock, then commit it
uv run fastapi dev {{ package_name }}/main.py   # auto-reloading development server
```

Open <http://localhost:8000/docs> for interactive API documentation and
<http://localhost:8000/health> for the health check.

## Configuration

Settings live in `{{ package_name }}/core/config.py`. Override any of them with an environment
variable prefixed `{{ package_name|upper }}_`, or copy `.env.example` to `.env` for local values.
`.env` is git-ignored; never commit it.

In production, set `{{ package_name|upper }}_ENVIRONMENT=production` and list the real
`{{ package_name|upper }}_ALLOWED_HOSTS` and `{{ package_name|upper }}_CORS_ORIGINS`; wildcards are rejected there.

## Development

| Task | Command |
| --- | --- |
| Run tests with coverage | `uv run pytest` |
| Lint | `uv run ruff check .` |
| Format | `uv run ruff format .` |
| Type-check | `uv run mypy {{ package_name }}` |
| Serve without reload | `uv run {{ package_name }} serve` |
| Build sdist and wheel | `uv build` |
| Install git hooks | `uvx pre-commit install` |

## Container

```bash
docker build -t {{ project_name }} .
docker run --rm -p 8000:8000 {{ project_name }}
```

## Project layout

```
{{ package_name }}/
  main.py          # application factory, /health, router registration
  routers/         # HTTP endpoints (thin)
  models.py        # SQLModel table model and API schemas
  db.py            # engine and per-request session dependency
  core/config.py   # typed settings
  core/exceptions.py, core/middleware.py
tests/             # pytest suite with an isolated in-memory database
```

